  "notes": "Improves the nine-copy H-type upper bound from 18 to 17; log_2(17)/9 = 0.4541625379, without improving the published asymptotic exponent log_2(3)/4. The original certificate uses unnormalized (|0>+exp(i*pi/4)|1>)^9 and QlAb stabilizers, with partition (3,3,3). This witness applies (SH)^9 and adjusts canonical phases and norms to reproduce the challenge target (cos(pi/8)|0>+sin(pi/8)|1>)^9. For one normalized copy, SH|T> = exp(i*pi/8)|H>. Search: seed 4, 1200 iterations, destroy sizes (1,2,3,4), repair shortlist 2, epochs 200, temperatures 0.005 to 0.0002. The successful run took about 16.5 seconds; aggregate costs of preceding searches were not recorded. The original exact decomposition is preserved at research/constructions/data/t_product_n9_rank17_stabzoo.json. All 512 amplitudes are checked exactly after conversion.",
